    "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix",
    "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ -5x+6y=7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
